# Task outputs and verification contract

## Rule

A task describes an objective and acceptance expectations, not a copied catalog of applicable rules. Generated deliverables first enter `outputs/<task-id>/`. Tests, static analysis, documentation and review evidence are kept alongside the candidate as appropriate.

A successful task execution is not by itself a successful QA Gate or an approved release. Failed or inconclusive controls must be reported. A separate approved process moves eligible product artifacts into `release/`; this process can be manual or automatic and need not leave an internal transfer log inside `release/`.
